                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Morristown TN",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 5 at 8:57AM EST until November 5 at 11:00AM EST by NWS Morristown TN",
                "description": "FFWMRX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Morristown has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSoutheastern Polk County in east Tennessee...\n\n* Until 1100 AM EST.\n\n* At 857 AM EST, Local law enforcement reported widespread\ncatastrophic flash flooding was still ongoing with numerous\nbusinesses and homes under several feet of water.\n\nFLASH FLOOD EMERGENCY for Copperhill. This is a PARTICULARLY\nDANGEROUS SITUATION. SEEK HIGHER GROUND NOW!\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...This is a PARTICULARLY DANGEROUS SITUATION. SEEK HIGHER\nGROUND NOW! Life threatening flash flooding of low water\ncrossings, small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nDucktown and Copperhill.",
                "instruction": "Move to higher ground now! This is an extremely dangerous and\nlife-threatening situation. Do not attempt to travel unless you are\nfleeing an area subject to flooding or under an evacuation order.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
