                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Peachtree City GA",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 5 at 8:57AM EST until November 5 at 11:00AM EST by NWS Peachtree City GA",
                "description": "FFWFFC\n\nThe National Weather Service in Peachtree City has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNorth Central Fannin County in north central Georgia...\n\n* Until 1100 AM EST.\n\n* At 857 AM EST, emergency management reported significant flooding\nin and around McCaysville. No additional rainfall is expected, but\nflooding impacts will continue.\n\nFLASH FLOOD EMERGENCY for McCaysville. This is a PARTICULARLY\nDANGEROUS SITUATION. SEEK HIGHER GROUND NOW!\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Emergency management reported.\n\nIMPACT...This is a PARTICULARLY DANGEROUS SITUATION. SEEK HIGHER\nGROUND NOW! Life threatening flash flooding of low water\ncrossings, small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMcCaysville and nearby areas of North Central Fannin County.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nHothouse Creek, Toccoa River, Ocoee River and Fightingtown Creek.",
                "instruction": "Move to higher ground now! This is an extremely dangerous and\nlife-threatening situation. Do not attempt to travel unless you are\nfleeing an area subject to flooding or under an evacuation order.\n\nTurn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
